o was watching the webcam saw me  someone who was not my boyfriend who  also was watching and someone in New  York saw what was happening and they  called the paramedics and they came and  they carried me out mmm I spent three  days in the ICU unconscious  my parents found out what had happened  because my ex-husband called them and  when I finally woke up three days later  attached to all these beeping things all  these machines my mom was sitting at the  foot of the bed and the first thing I  thought when I woke up was not oh my god  I tried to kill myself Here I am in the  in the hospital it was my parents spent  so much money that they don't have to  get here to be with me why would they do  something so expensive for someone so  undeserving and the first thing I said  when I woke up was I'm sorry for how  expensive this is I'm sorry I cost you  money I'm sorry I'm sorry I'm sorry I'm  sorry I'm sorry  apologizing used to be what gave me the  only kind of skin that I had I started  calling myself the cheese grater girl  early on because I felt like I didn't  have any kind of barrier between me and  the world  I felt like anything could get in and  infect me and the one shield I had was  to apologize over and over and over  again I'm sorry for existing I'm sorry  for being ugly I'm sorry for being fat  I'm sorry for not being good enough to  date I'm sorry I'm sorry I'm sorry I'm  not the last girl like I'm not as good  as your last girlfriend I'm sorry I'm  too fat I'm too ugly  anything that I could possibly apologize  for I would apologize for Ani DiFranco  who I mentioned earlier saint ani says  every tool is a weapon if you hold it  right and that's apologies were both my  tool and my weapon  they were my way of putting a barrier  between me and other people because if  you apologize enough people don't in  fact forgive you they get sick of you  and they stop wanting to hear it because  they know that no matter how much you  apologize it's just gonna happen 