er to build myself a skin  I have never I'll be 43 years old  tomorrow and I have never thought  anything about me was in any way  beautiful except this because now I have  a barrier and I can look at this and I  can see the color and I can know that  that means that my skin is separate from  the outside world and that it actually  can't be gotten into when I would come  into DBT with a new tattoo my therapist  would always inevitably say tell me  again how this isn't self-injury so if  you're treating with someone if you're a  DBT therapist and you're treating  someone like me who feels the need to do  something like this what I want to  finish by asking you is just to please  be slow to pathologize difference  because we have our own ways of coping  outside of you but we're using what you  teach us it's just that sometimes we  interpret it in sort of interesting ways  so that said I'll shut up I'll let you  ask me questions and thank you thank you  for letting me be here  you
 

